diff --git a/Documentation/admin-guide/namespaces/uts-views.rst b/Documentation/admin-guide/namespaces/uts-views.rst
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..be34ceca6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/admin-guide/namespaces/uts-views.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,117 @@
+.. SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
+
+Native UTS instance views
+=========================
+
+CONFIG_UTS_NS_VIEWS adds an optional host-managed resource domain to native
+procfs and sysfs. It requires UTS resources, PID/net/time namespaces, cgroup
+v2, PSI, and an ARM64 or x86 host. SELinux is independent of this facility.
+Unconfigured UTS namespaces retain ordinary kernel behavior.
+
+Configuration and lifetime
+--------------------------
+
+Only CAP_SYS_ADMIN in the initial user and PID namespaces may configure a
+noninitial UTS namespace. First bind its cgroup with NS_UTS_BIND_RESOURCES,
+then bind its device projection and netns with NS_UTS_BIND_EVENTS, and set
+the time namespace offsets. NS_UTS_CONFIG_VIEW accepts ABI 1, zero flags
+and reserved bytes, the same generation, and PID/net/time namespace FDs.
+The layout is 4304 bytes on native and compat tasks. String fields have
+zero padding and no control characters; cmdline must be nonempty.
+
+The boottime offset must be the negative Run origin. The monotonic offset
+must represent an origin in the same Run, with an elapsed suspend offset
+between zero and the kernel's current suspend offset. These offsets are
+immutable after association, including in descendant time namespaces.
+
+A successful configuration is published once. Reconfiguration returns
+EBUSY; GET_VIEW reports the existing state for recovery. Its 128-byte
+response carries immutable namespace IDs, generation, cgroup, profile
+SHA-256 and an instance boot UUID. BOUND and LIVE are separate bits.
+Capabilities report the implemented interfaces. Initial namespaces may
+not be supplied as instance PID/net/time namespaces. Malformed parameters
+return EINVAL and namespace permission failures return EPERM.
+
+UTS descendants share the resource domain. PID/time descendants inherit
+ownership; guest setns cannot cross resource domains. Namespace objects,
+proc mounts and sysfs superblocks hold references. The domain does not
+hold references to those namespaces, avoiding a netns/event socket cycle.
+The instance init exit, cgroup root removal or disappearance of a pinned
+device revokes LIVE. Subsequent resource access returns ENODEV. Ordinary
+thread and descendant cgroup exit do not revoke the domain.
+
+Mounts and filesystem behavior
+-----------------------------
+
+Mount proc/sysfs only after CONFIG_VIEW. A bootstrap mount created before
+configuration still denotes its original filesystem. The host launcher
+must remove it, and any raw host mount/directory/namespace FDs, before
+running Android. This is a launcher's responsibility; UTS does not revoke
+privileges the host explicitly hands to a guest.
+
+Each proc superblock pins its resource domain and UTS identity; its PID
+namespace must belong to that domain. New and traditional mount APIs
+perform the same check. A retained FD keeps its original source even if
+the reading task enters another namespace. Dynamic seq files retain
+normal read/seek semantics without a userspace cache.
+
+Resource files and raw sysinfo use the same root cgroup accounting.
+Per-CPU user/nice/system counters come from rstat subtree data, including
+removed descendants. Context-switch and fork counters use the same rstat
+propagation. Their scheduler accounting remains disabled until the first
+native view is configured. No physical interrupt is assigned, so IRQ
+counters are zero and IRQ names are absent. Swap, disk and buddy device
+lists are empty rather than exposing host devices. Slab totals remain
+available in meminfo but physical slab object lists are empty.
+
+VM refault/reclaim counters and a virtual Node 0/Normal zone are supplied
+for LMKD. MemAvailable is the resource ABI's bounded reclaim estimate.
+The VM zone is an instance model, not physical NUMA/DRAM topology. PSI
+read, trigger writes, poll and release share the instance PSI group.
+
+Global proc entries are explicitly classified in fs/proc/native.c.
+Unclassified driver or firmware entries are absent from both lookup and
+readdir. PID/net interfaces retain their ordinary permissions. Generic
+proc chmod/chown changes stay in this superblock rather than rewriting
+global proc_dir_entry metadata. Sysctl permits ordinary network/UTS
+semantics and selected compatible reads. Global writes with no instance
+implementation fail explicitly; they are not accepted as no-ops.
+
+Sysfs uses a private kernfs root with standard sysfs magic, attributes,
+links, ownership, xattrs and SELinux genfs labeling. CPU IDs follow the
+instance cpuset intersected with online CPUs. Network objects are tagged
+with their actual netns and updated by netdevice notifications. Device
+class/dev-char links remain inside the private root. Only explicitly
+bound DRM/V4L2 devices are created; their device objects are pinned.
+GPU bus selection and PCI IDs needed by drivers are retained, while host
+platform addresses and DT ancestors are not exported.
+
+Device uevent action writes emit normal NETLINK_KOBJECT_UEVENT messages
+only to the instance netns, using the same mapping as runtime events.
+They do not call the physical device's uevent store. Ordinary socket,
+socketcall and io_uring APIs are unchanged. No private AOSP view protocol
+or filesystem-label exception is required.
+
+A device FD still exposes its real driver's ioctl capabilities. Native
+file views do not promise to virtualize DRM/V4L2 hardware ioctl identity,
+CPU ISA/HWCAP, or privileged raw CPU instructions. Android SELinux remains
+responsible for app mount permissions. Enforcing, permissive and disabled
+modes require separate integration tests, as do Mesa and codec backends.
+
+Validation
+----------
+
+Build tools/testing/selftests/uts_views, then run uts_views as host root
+on a disposable test system with a writable unified cgroup hierarchy and
+cpu, memory, cpuset, pids and io delegated into it. The test uses separate
+PID/mount/UTS/net/time namespaces, two memory limits, fixed FDs, remounts,
+PSI triggers, descendant netns and init-exit invalidation. If card0 exists,
+it also validates an authorized DRM projection and standard coldboot.
+An optional first argument names an ARM32 helper inherited with UTS FD 9;
+this permits native/compat ioctl validation on an ARM64 kernel. Tests need
+CAP_SYS_ADMIN and CAP_SYS_TIME in the host and deliberately create load in
+their temporary cgroups. A missing kernel extension returns kselftest SKIP.
+
+These checks do not certify complete Android boot, SELinux policy labels,
+LMKD pressure handling, GPU/codec compatibility or isolation performance.
+Those require the target board and the final launcher/image integration.
